		(uuid "f6cc9e80-b78e-47fc-a7b3-ecc5e66a0608")
	)
	(text "BOM DEFAULTS (unless noted on the part)\n• R: 1 % thick film 0603, 0.1 W, 75 V (Yageo RC0603FR-07). Tolerance shown only where it matters.\n• C: dielectric and voltage rating shown under the value.\n• Every part carries Manufacturer_Name / Manufacturer_Part_Number / Supplier (+ Mouser or supplier PN)\n   fields -> BOM + baskets in Docs/BOM/ (2026-10-03)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 262.89 138.176 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fd5c63fb-fb4c-49d1-9a96-88473f91c6d5")
	)
	(text "J9 → U23 (ch 9–16)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 17.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ff707caf-5421-404c-a4fb-9943006e8fe8")
	)
	(text_box "INPUT NETWORK & NOISE (per channel)\n• Electrode (active, OPA376 buffer) → Rfilt 4k99 → INxP ; Cdiff → SRB1 (= reference, internal IN–).\n• Differential C (not C to GND): CMRR independent of part tolerance (SBAS499 §10.2).\n• fc = 1/(2π·2·Rfilt·Cdiff). The delta-sigma only needs attenuation near fMOD = 1.024 MHz\n   → EEG band set digitally (HP 0.5 Hz, 50 Hz notch, LP).\n• TPD1E05U06: unidirectional ESD, ≤ 10 nA leakage @ 2.5 V; pin 1 = signal, pin 2 = GND; place at the connector.\n• Input range ±VREF/gain = ±187.5 mV @ gain 24 → electrode DC offset must stay inside.\n• Lead-off current sees the buffer output, not the skin → check contact via the 50 Hz level / at the electrode.\n• Cdiff = 2.2 nF C0G 1 % (was 20 nF): fc = 1/(2π·2·4k99·2.2 nF) ≈ 7.2 kHz;\n   crosstalk via the shared R51 ≈ 2π·f·Cdiff·R51 ≈ 0.35 % (–49 dB) @ 50 Hz (was 3 %)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 222 0)
		(size 96.52 19.3)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b5438624-834b-4d66-88d2-801c73e35045")
	)
	(text_box "SUPPLIES & DECOUPLING\n• AVDD = +5V_ADC (LT3042, 5.00 V; allowed 4.75–5.25 V), AVSS = GND (unipolar). DVDD = +3V3 (buck; allowed 1.8–3.6 V). AVDD – DVDD ≤ 3.6 V.\n• VCAP1 100 µF, VCAP2 1 µF, VCAP3 1 µF ∥ 100 nF, VCAP4 1 µF: internal regulator bypass (datasheet pin table). Place at the pins.\n• Datasheet: 1 µF on every AVDD pin (19, 21, 22, 56, 59), pin 59 cap returned to pin 58 (charge pump), AVDD1 54 → 1 µF to AVSS1 53, DVDD 1 µF.\n• Single ground plane; AVSS and DGND joined under the ADS1299 (§12.1)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 261.62 116.84 0)
		(size 143.635 11.605)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bd8c0616-79f2-4515-9d9e-7b115657f825")
	)
	(text_box "ADS1299 ×2 – CONFIGURATION (TI SBAS499C)\n• Cascaded mode (§10.1.4.1): SCLK / DIN / DOUT shared, CS1 → U6, CS2 → U23. DOUT is high-Z when CS is high. DAISY_IN → DGND.\n• Clock: U6 CLKSEL = 1 + CONFIG1.CLK_EN = 1 → 2.048 MHz on CLK; U23 CLKSEL = 0 runs from it. START shared → simultaneous sampling.\n• DRDY from U6 only → MCU EXTI (falling edge) → read U6 (CS1) then U23 (CS2).\n• Referential montage: MISC1.SRB1 = 1 (SRB1 → all IN–). Unused INxN tied to AVDD (§10.1.1). SRB2, BIASREF, BIASIN open.\n• Reference: internal 4.5 V, CONFIG3.PD_REFBUF = 1. VREFP 10 µF ∥ 100 nF to VREFN = AVSS.\n• Control lines: R86 PWDN, R87 RESET, R88 CS1, R90 CS2 → 10k to DVDD; R89 START → 10k to GND (idle while the MCU boots).\n• GPIO1 unused → 10k to DGND (R66, R84). RESV1 → DGND. NC / RESERVED open.\n• Power-up (§11.1): AVDD + DVDD stable → wait tPOR = 2^18 tCLK ≈ 128 ms (and VCAP1 > 1.1 V) → RESET pulse ≥ 2 tCLK\n   → wait 18 tCLK → SDATAC → write registers → START. Analog inputs must stay low until the supplies are up\n   (+5V_UGA for the electrode buffers starts only after +5V_ADC PG)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 261.62 95 0)
		(size 143.38 20.57)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e4faa757-af38-4cad-a4ce-98dba3288263")
	)
